What Slows Buyers Down (and How to Avoid It)
Even well-intentioned buyers can unknowingly slow their own process down. Common culprits include:
    • Waiting until after finding a home to start the mortgage conversation 
    • Making large purchases or opening new credit during the loan process 
    • Submitting incomplete documentation, which creates delays in underwriting 
    • Not understanding rate lock timing, leading to last-minute rate changes 
Avoiding these missteps can shave meaningful time off your path to closing — sometimes the difference between missing out on a home and getting the keys.
